  "text": "Nessa is the mother of the Ulster king Concobar mac Nessa. The Druid Cathbad lusted after the studious maiden Assa, whose name meant gentle. He had her tutors killed to reach her. The violence made the girl a fighter, and she then took the name Nessa, which meant ungentle. Cathbad did not give up. He surprised Nessa at her bath, the one time she lacked her weapons, and raped her. He then kept her as his hostage and concubine. Nessa outwitted him. Skilled at reading omens, she spied a worm drifting in a cup of wine. She knew it would make her bear a hero, so she swallowed it. From that conceiving came Concobar mac Nessa, the king. In later years Cathbad schooled Concobar's fighter Cuchulainn and fathered the heroine Findchoem, who used the same method. Cathbad also appeared in the tale of Deirdre, whose birth he said would bring sorrow to Ulster.",
